Software Engineer - Java &lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;No Spacing&quot;&gt;Work on the mission-critical Java back end&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;25&quot; data-local-id=&quot;079e1865-d4ef-42fd-b7e7-cc9e402e3857&quot;&gt;At Schuberg Philis, we don’t just deliver IT solutions, we design, build, and run mission-critical systems that our customers rely on every single day. From infrastructure to cloud-native platforms, every layer of technology is crafted with one goal in mind: uncompromising reliability and excellence. We take pride in working shoulder-to-shoulder with our customers, ensuring their most vital operations run smoothly, no matter how complex the challenge.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;482&quot; data-local-id=&quot;c00a1f72-3107-4ff3-91be-891f21ef9d80&quot;&gt;We are looking for an experienced Java Software Engineer to work with one of our biggest banking customers, delivering business value using cloud technologies and a DevOps way of working.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;671&quot; data-local-id=&quot;6212e011-4dd4-4f56-9dbd-0d263b9dc82c&quot;&gt;As a Java software engineer, you will be responsible for the development of core business features for our customer and for improving its software delivery capabilities, working closely with internal stakeholders and other DevOps teams. You will work daily within a DevOps team where your colleagues will expect you to maintain a wide overview while guarding aspects like quality, security, and planning.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;671&quot; data-local-id=&quot;6212e011-4dd4-4f56-9dbd-0d263b9dc82c&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;What-you’ll-do&quot; data-local-id=&quot;38e10f4a-b9e9-44b3-a739-b8374f17367b&quot; data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1078&quot;&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1096&quot; data-local-id=&quot;af7e8743-fa2d-432e-81d7-032ce76f3962&quot;&gt;Design, build and run Java-based micro-services and APIs that support business‑critical banking processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1096&quot; data-local-id=&quot;af7e8743-fa2d-432e-81d7-032ce76f3962&quot;&gt;Work end-to-end: from clarifying requirements and refining user stories to development, testing, deployment and operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1331&quot; data-local-id=&quot;5a328879-58d8-4ca5-b732-2cd1b0e57d41&quot;&gt;Collaborate closely with other DevOps teams, architects and business stakeholders to deliver secure, reliable and scalable solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1467&quot; data-local-id=&quot;349c98d5-71ea-4ba6-9aec-3f5357fe43a3&quot;&gt;Contribute to improving engineering practices: code quality, testing, CI/CD pipelines, monitoring, and automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1584&quot; data-local-id=&quot;fdcba0d5-1ea9-41b0-afb7-4337e3ab1f15&quot;&gt;Help the team keep production stable, with a strong focus on reliability, security, observability and incident prevention&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1709&quot; data-local-id=&quot;494978a8-a68f-4e24-b793-f3678b1c02be&quot;&gt;Stay up to date with modern engineering practices and bring in ideas to improve the platform and the way we work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1972&quot; data-local-id=&quot;f96e317b-5ecd-4d5b-8476-5c5dfd22720c&quot;&gt;Ideally, you have:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1994&quot; data-local-id=&quot;6ec3c441-8055-41ab-bc28-4225542be6bc&quot;&gt;Strong hands-on Java experience (preferably Java 17+)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2051&quot; data-local-id=&quot;27d118e0-1aff-4218-b64c-865f96c54f5e&quot;&gt;Solid experience with Spring Boot&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2088&quot; data-local-id=&quot;09b8457d-aafa-4cc7-8f36-e72cf4537876&quot;&gt;Experience designing and building RESTful APIs and system integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2162&quot; data-local-id=&quot;f740c046-43e8-4fe4-b84f-d974c211b5e7&quot;&gt;Experience with Java-based microservices in production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2220&quot; data-local-id=&quot;bb77d7a9-0719-497d-8e81-1cc55df16d60&quot;&gt;A track record of writing testable, maintainable, high-quality code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2291&quot; data-local-id=&quot;e1dec140-43a1-4fa5-b8e7-e440ee656638&quot;&gt;Experience working in a professional development team (code reviews, CI/CD, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2291&quot; data-local-id=&quot;e1dec140-43a1-4fa5-b8e7-e440ee656638&quot;&gt;We’re also open to engineers with a strong background in other languages (e.g. Kotlin, .NET, C++)&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;plus&lt;/strong&gt; at least ~3 years of recent, hands-on Java experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;No Spacing&quot;&gt;What would be a great plus for us?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You don’t need all of these. Having some of them – or strong interest and the ability to learn – is a plus:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2658&quot; data-local-id=&quot;f65048ba-e98a-42ec-b06a-0570991d4109&quot;&gt;Experience with Kotlin or other JVM languages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2707&quot; data-local-id=&quot;8be92de5-fba9-43c8-85e3-9199a10e65a9&quot;&gt;Knowledge of Authentication and Authorization protocols (OIDC / OAuth2, etc)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2787&quot; data-local-id=&quot;6c5926df-41c1-4f93-8fe5-50e9beeb606e&quot;&gt;Experience with DevOps practices and tools (preferably Azure DevOps)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2859&quot; data-local-id=&quot;5a679d47-07e8-4548-a9b8-e83a4d4ca58c&quot;&gt;Experience with public cloud (AWS and/or Azure)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2910&quot; data-local-id=&quot;231c3782-80a4-47f4-8ba9-2d67216b56e0&quot;&gt;Infrastructure as Code experience (e.g. Terraform)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2964&quot; data-local-id=&quot;1673f1c9-d2ec-4b40-8191-a1f11e526c6d&quot;&gt;Experience working in Agile/Scrum teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Everyone we work with and consider working with has a right to equal treatment. The hiring and appraisal process at Schuberg Philis is designed to be thorough and equitable, implementing fair payment, benefits, and opportunities across all demographics.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;It is our desire to be a company that brings together multiple nationalities, cultures, religions, genders, abilities, and talents within and across our teams. We welcome colleagues from diverse backgrounds to join Schuberg Philis and actively support diversity and inclusion in the tech industry.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a> Technology  Schiphol-Rijk

Corporate Development Director &lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id=&quot;an-overview-of-this-role&quot; data-lfile-container=&quot;21ea07e5-ded4-47e8-ad92-4ca7b7d6be35&quot; data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Corporate Development Director, you&#39;ll help influence how GitLab invests to win: what we build, what we buy, where we partner, and what we should not pursue. This role sits within the Corporate Development &amp;amp; Strategic Partnerships team, reporting to the VP, Corporate Development &amp;amp; Strategic Partnerships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role straddles strategy and M&amp;amp;A engagements. You&#39;ll lead research that frames GitLab&#39;s options: mapping the markets in and around our AI-powered DevSecOps platform, testing where we have a right to win, and turning that into clear recommendations for the executive team. When the answer is to acquire, you&#39;ll drive the deal process end to end, from outreach through close and integration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Success here is not measured by deal count. It looks like sharper strategic choices: a well-reasoned point of view on our priority markets, investment theses that product and executive leaders rely on, acquisitions that speed up the roadmap when buying is the right answer, and an educated no when it isn&#39;t. You&#39;ll own the wider market perspective rather than individual product categories, and work with the team&#39;s Analyst on the research behind it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;strategy-and-research&quot;&gt;Strategy and research&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the wider market view.&lt;/strong&gt; Research the broader market GitLab competes in, beyond specific product categories: competitive dynamics, AI-native entrants, technology shifts and where value is moving. Collaborate with the team&#39;s Analyst on the research and turn the findings into a clear point of view on where GitLab should play.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build an investment thesis for each focus area.&lt;/strong&gt; Work with Product and Engineering leaders to define the problems worth solving, the capabilities GitLab needs, and what it would cost in time and money to get there on our own.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the competitive and landscape view.&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain market maps and a current read on GitLab&#39;s competitors: their strategy, product direction, positioning, pricing, and M&amp;amp;A and funding activity. Produce competitor analyses that show where we lead, where we&#39;re exposed and how rivals are likely to move. Flag shifts by competitors, hyperscalers and AI labs that change our options, and bring the implications to Product and the executive team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define where GitLab should not play.&lt;/strong&gt; Identify adjacencies that dilute focus and markets where the economics or competition work against us. Make the case for a no with the same rigor as a yes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;build-buy-or-partner&quot;&gt;Build, buy or partner&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Run the build, buy, partner analysis.&lt;/strong&gt; For each strategic gap, compare the options side by side on speed, cost, risk, control and strategic fit, and bring a clear recommendation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deliver strategic clarity to&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;executives and the Board.&lt;/strong&gt; Produce short strategy memos/decks and business cases that set out the decision, the trade-offs and what we give up with each path.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Feed company strategy and planning.&lt;/strong&gt; Bring an outside-in view of the market and the inorganic options available into annual and long-range planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work hand in hand with Strategic Partnerships.&lt;/strong&gt; When partnering is the right answer, frame the opportunity and hand it to the partnership owner with a clear thesis. When it isn&#39;t, explain why.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;deal-execution-and-integration&quot;&gt;Deal execution and integration&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own end-to-end deal process management.&lt;/strong&gt; Validate target fit against GitLab&#39;s our target profile, product roadmap and other criteria, and build the acquisition rationale and business case. Drive our M&amp;amp;A process from intro call through the various steps through to closing and integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Evaluate the deal.&lt;/strong&gt; Develop valuation, commercial integrity assessment, impact on GitLab&#39;s business and provide negotiations assistance to the VP and the executive team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead cross-functional diligence.&lt;/strong&gt; Run pre-LOI validation and diligence across Product, Engineering, Security, Finance, Legal and People, and communicate findings clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive deal documents with Legal.&lt;/strong&gt; Prepare NDAs, LOIs and purchase agreements with GitLab Legal and outside counsel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own integration outcomes.&lt;/strong&gt; Lead post-acquisition integration as the DRI, measured against the roadmap and business goals in the business case. Bring lessons learned back into the strategy work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build the external network.&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain relationships with founders, executives, investors, bankers and advisors that bring us early insight and pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-bring&quot;&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategy and deal experience.&lt;/strong&gt; 8+ years across corporate development, corporate strategy, strategy consulting or technology investing, including 5+ years leading acquisitions end to end in enterprise software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Structured strategic thinking.&lt;/strong&gt; You form a point of view from incomplete information, test it against data, and change your mind when the evidence says so. You&#39;re as comfortable recommending that we stay out of a market as that we enter it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Market research depth.&lt;/strong&gt; Skilled in market sizing, competitive analysis and landscape mapping, and in turning research into a recommendation, not a report.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deal craft.&lt;/strong&gt; Skilled in valuation, financial modeling, deal structuring, negotiation and integration planning, with experience across varied consideration structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical fluency.&lt;/strong&gt; A working understanding of software development, DevSecOps and the AI landscape, enough to hold substantive conversations with product and engineering leaders about roadmaps and architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clear executive communication.&lt;/strong&gt; You write short, decision-ready updates and present trade-offs plainly to executives and the Board, in an async-first environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Influence without authority.&lt;/strong&gt; You build trust across Product, Engineering, Finance and Legal and move decisions forward across functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ownership with collaboration.&lt;/strong&gt; You own the strategic view and the recommendation, and partner closely with the team&#39;s Analyst on research and analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred:&lt;/strong&gt; familiarity with the DevSecOps, security, AI and open source ecosystems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You value the &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/company/culture/all-remote/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;all remote&lt;/a&gt; lifestyle and share our &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/values/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;values&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Corporate Development &amp;amp; Strategic Partnerships team helps GitLab decide how to grow beyond what we build on our own. We own inorganic strategy: acquisitions, strategic partnerships with hyperscalers and AI labs, and the research that tells us which to pursue and which to pass on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We work across Product, Engineering, Finance, Legal and the executive group. We set direction and do the detailed work ourselves, with a high degree of ownership and transparency in a fully remote, asynchronous environment.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot;&gt;Benefits to support your health, finances, and well-being&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/time-off-and-absence/time-off-types/#flexible-paid-time-off-pto&quot;&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/company/culture/inclusion/tmrg-tmag/&quot;&gt;Team Member Resource Groups&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/stock-options/&quot;&gt;Equity Compensation &amp;amp; Employee Stock Purchase Plan&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/learning-and-development/growth-and-development/&quot;&gt;Growth and Development Fund&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/#parental-leave&quot;&gt;Parental Leave&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that we welcome interest from candidates with varying levels of experience; many successful candidates do not meet every single requirement. Additionally, studies have shown that people from &lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/company/culture/inclusion/#examples-of-select-underrepresented-groups&quot;&gt;underrepresented groups&lt;/a&gt; are less likely to apply to a job unless they meet every single qualification. If you&#39;re excited about this role, please apply and allow our recruiters to assess your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Country Hiring Guidelines: &lt;/strong&gt;GitLab hires new team members in countries around the world. All of our roles are remote, however some roles may carry specific location-based eligibility requirements. Our Talent Acquisition team can help answer any questions about location after starting the recruiting process.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy: &lt;/strong&gt;Please review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/candidate-faq/recruitment-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt; Your privacy is important to us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GitLab is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. GitLab’s policies and practices relating to recruitment, employment, career development and advancement, promotion, and retirement are based solely on merit, regardless of race, color, religion, ancestry, sex (including pregnancy, lactation, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression), national origin, age, citizenship, marital status, mental or physical disability, genetic information (including family medical history), discharge status from the military, protected veteran status (which includes disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active duty wartime or campaign badge veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans), or any other basis protected by law. GitLab will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. See also&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#equal-employment-opportunity-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;GitLab’s EEO Policy&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/labor-and-employment-notices/#eeoc-us-equal-employment-opportunity-commission-notices&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO is the Law&lt;/a&gt;. If you have a disability or special need that requires&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#reasonable-accommodation&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation&lt;/a&gt;, please let us know during the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/interviewing/#adjustments-to-our-interview-process&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;recruiting process&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a> Corporate Affairs  Remote

Teamleiter Fahrzeugbewertung - Großraum Hamburg (m/w/d) &lt;p&gt;Du willst keine Führungsrolle am Schreibtisch. Du willst ein Team, das du im Feld kennst, und Fahrzeuge, die du selbst in der Hand hattest. Als Teamleiter Fahrzeugbewertung für Norddeutschland führst du die Bewerter deiner Region, prüfst ihre Berichte stichprobenartig und stehst an den Tagen, an denen es zählt, selbst mit am Fahrzeug.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Standort:&lt;/strong&gt; Hamburg – Du arbeitest eigenständig in deiner Region im Außendienst und verantwortest Norddeutschland.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Über uns&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CarOnSale ist die KI-gestützte Plattform für den B2B-Gebrauchtwagenhandel in Europa. Über 40.000 Käufer aus mehr als 20 Ländern handeln auf unserer Plattform – und 85 % des Inventars ist exklusiv bei uns. Wir verbinden Software, Pricing-Intelligenz, Logistik und Finanzierung in einer Schicht – als Betriebssystem für eine ganze Branche.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;One Platform. One Profit Engine.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Deine Aufgaben&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team und Qualität&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du führst die Fahrzeugbewerter deiner Region und bist ihr erster Ansprechpartner bei Fahrzeugaufnahme, Kundenkontakt und Prozessfragen&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du sicherst unsere Qualitätsstandards und entwickelst sie weiter&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du prüfst Berichte und Bewertungen stichprobenartig, analysierst Reklamationen und leitest daraus konkrete Maßnahmen ab&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du steuerst dein Team über Kennzahlen, ziehst daraus Schlüsse und machst sie im Management sichtbar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Entwicklung deines Teams&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du führst regelmäßige 1:1-Gespräche, in denen offen gesprochen und gemeinsam nachgeschärft wird&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du verantwortest das Onboarding neuer Teammitglieder und gibst dein Fachwissen weiter&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bewertung vor Ort&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du bist regelmäßig selbst bei Fahrzeugaufnahmen dabei und arbeitest mit unserer Bewertungstechnologie&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du bist das Gesicht von CarOnSale beim Händler: sicheres Auftreten, Gespräche auf Augenhöhe, professioneller Eindruck&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Was du mitbringst&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Abgeschlossene technische Ausbildung im Kfz-Bereich, zum Beispiel als Kfz-Meister, Kfz-Mechatroniker, Fahrzeuglackierer oder Karosserie- und Fahrzeugbaumechaniker&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mindestens ein Jahr Erfahrung in der Führung eines Teams, verbunden mit der Bereitschaft, selbst mit anzupacken&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Erfahrung mit Fahrzeugbewertungen, Gutachten oder Zustandsprüfungen und ein Auge für Details&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sicherer Umgang mit Kennzahlen: du erkennst Muster, ziehst Schlüsse und stellst sie klar dar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sicheres, professionelles Auftreten im Kundenkontakt und unternehmerisches Denken&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deutsch auf C2-Niveau&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Führerschein der Klasse B&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;KI-affine Arbeitsweise: du nutzt digitale Tools aktiv, um deine Arbeit und die deines Teams besser zu machen&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Von Vorteil&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Erfahrung in der Steuerung eines regional verteilten Teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Englisch auf B2-Niveau&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Was dich bei uns erwartet&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Firmenwagen zur privaten Nutzung&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unlimitierte Tankkarte&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Laptop und Diensthandy für dein Office on the road&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;28 Tage Urlaub&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2× jährliches Karriere- &amp;amp; Entwicklungsgespräch&lt;/li&gt;
